available. Let me think about what the user wants:\n\nThe user wants to raise the priority of all alarms associated with temperature points (those containing \"Temp\") to \"high\".\n\nSince I don't have a tool to list alarms, I'll need to make some assumptions. Let me check what alarm-related tools are available:\n\n- create_analog_alarm - Create an analog alarm\n- create_digital_alarm - Create a digital alarm\n- set_threshold - Update threshold on an analog alarm\n- enable_alarm / disable_alarm / delete_alarm\n\nThere's no \"list_alarms\" tool available. So I can't look up existing alarms. But I know there are two points: Temp_A and Temp_B (both analog).\n\nThe user says \"把所有带Temp的温度点的报警优先级都提高到high\" - meaning \"Raise the priority of all alarms on temperature points with 'Temp' in their name to high.\"\n\nSince I don't have a way to list existing alarms, I should ask the user which alarms already exist on these temperature points. But wait - maybe I can try to infer. Let me first ask the user if there are existing alarms, or I could just create new alarms with high priority if none exist.\n\nActually, let me re-read the user's request more carefully: \"把所有带Temp的温度点的报警优先级都提高到high\" - this implies there ARE existing alarms that need their priority changed to \"high\".\n\nBut looking at the tools, there's no \"update alarm priority\" tool. The `set_threshold` tool only updates high_limit, low_limit, and deadband - not priority. And the `create_analog_alarm` tool has a priority parameter, but that's for creation.\n\nHmm, I don't have a tool to change the priority of an existing alarm. Let me think about this differently.\n\nActually, looking more carefully, I don't have a tool to change the priority of an alarm. The available alarm-related tools are:\n- create_analog_alarm\n- create_digital_alarm\n- set_threshold (only updates limits and deadband)\n- enable_alarm\n- disable_alarm\n- delete_alarm\n\nNone of these allow changing priority of an existing alarm. \n\nSo my options are:\n1. If alarms already exist and need priority changed - I can't do that with available tools. I should inform the user.\n2. If no alarms exist yet - I could create new alarms with high priority.\n\nLet me ask the user whether alarms already exist on these points."}], "rag": {"enabled": false, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 12, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": false, "selected_workflow": null}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 15275, "output_tokens": 841, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 10977.628700000423}, "judge": null}
