details directly. Let me think...\n\nI don't have a tool to list widgets on a page or get details of a specific widget. Let me check the available tools again...\n\nThe available tools don't include a \"list_widgets\" or \"get_widget\" function. So I can't directly inspect the valve1 widget on source_page.\n\nHowever, the user says to \"copy\" the valve1 from source_page to target_page. Since I don't have a \"copy_widget\" tool either, I'll need to:\n1. Check what type/model valve1 is - but I can't inspect it.\n\nLet me think about what tools I have... I have `create_widget` which can create a widget. The user says \"复制\" (copy), so I need to recreate the widget on target_page with the same type and size, but at position [300, 120], and then bind it to VALVE_1_OPEN.\n\nSince I don't have a way to inspect the existing widget's properties (type, size, style, bindings), I should ask the user for the details of the valve1 widget on source_page.\n\nWait, let me reconsider. Perhaps the user just wants me to:\n1. Create a new widget of type \"pump\" or \"valve\" on target_page with the same type as valve1\n2. Bind it to VALVE_1_OPEN\n\nBut I don't know what type \"valve1\" is. I need to ask the user.\n\nActually, looking at the tool description for `create_widget`, the type can be things like 'thermometer', 'tank', 'pump', etc. A valve is likely a \"pump\" type or maybe there's a \"valve\" type. Let me check the description: \"type\": \"widget type, e.g. 'thermometer' / 'tank' / 'pump' / 'rect'\". So it could be \"pump\" or maybe just \"valve\".\n\nI don't have enough information to recreate the widget. Let me ask the user what type the valve1 widget is, and what size it should be."}], "rag": {"enabled": false, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 12, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": false, "selected_workflow": null}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 15341, "output_tokens": 818, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 8461.901399999988}, "judge": null}
